WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.575
Step six builds the GovCloud
request without sending it.

2
00:00:03.575 --> 00:00:07.862
You read the lab settings, change
the partition to A W S U S gov,

3
00:00:07.862 --> 00:00:10.400
and ask the kit for the live command.

4
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.251
It's describe events in u s gov west one,

5
00:00:13.251 --> 00:00:16.838
filtered to open and
upcoming events, as JSON.

6
00:00:16.838 --> 00:00:19.762
The region came from the
partition; you never typed it.

7
00:00:19.762 --> 00:00:23.962
Step seven asks for the details
of eleven events in one call.

8
00:00:23.962 --> 00:00:26.697
The kit refuses before anything runs:

9
00:00:26.697 --> 00:00:31.637
describe event details takes one to
ten event A R Ns, and it got eleven.

10
00:00:31.637 --> 00:00:34.764
In a live run the kit never
asks for more than ten,

11
00:00:34.764 --> 00:00:39.575
so this is the guard that keeps a coding
mistake from reaching AWS mid-run.

12
00:00:39.575 --> 00:00:44.272
Step eight runs this chapter's
tests, for the AWS Health block

13
00:00:44.272 --> 00:00:48.500
and the AWS rows of the live
tests: eleven pass, none fail.

14
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.400
Then delete the output folder.
